    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d318">

                <pb facs="0498" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg422"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/240: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-29T16:00:00-04:00">June 29, 1935—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>158. Department’s 385, October 10, 1934, 8 p.m.<anchor n="73" xml:id="d318-f1"/>
                    Please designate Johnson<anchor n="74" xml:id="d318-f2"/> or other member of
                    your staff to act as American representative at meeting of Governing body of
                    High Commission for German refugees to open in London July 17 in lieu of
                    Chamberlain who will not be present. In case technical questions involving
                    immigration should be raised you may call on a competent member of the consulate
                    general. This Government has no objection in principle to concentration of
                    general refugee work under League. No other instructions believed necessary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
